diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..f39bde3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,14 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## On-device article translation
+
+Use **Read in your language** above the news content to select a language, then choose **Translate**. This translates article headlines, summaries, captions, bodies, and teasers on the current page. **Show original** restores the English text and cancels any pending translation. Switching languages always starts from the English originals.
+
+Translation uses the browser's built-in [Translator API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/translator-api) in a secure context (HTTPS or localhost). Browser, device, and language-pair support are checked before translation. Unsupported browsers retain the original content and show an explanatory message. Language packs may require an initial download initiated by the Translate button; progress is displayed. Article text is processed on the device with no remote translation fallback.
+
+The control resets on navigation and releases its translator. Pages without article content do not show it. To include new editorial content, mark its container with `data-translate`; scripts, code, embedded controls, and `translate="no"` content are excluded. Text nodes are updated without replacing markup or inserting generated HTML.
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
